# Page objects

- One class per screen under `src/pages/{auth,brand,creator}/`. File name matches the class (`LoginPage.ts`).
- Extend `BasePage`. Sidebar and header come from `BasePage` composition — do not re-declare those locators.
- Settings sub-items are sections (in-place swap), not pages. Shared card/table/tab UI lives in `src/pages/shared/`.
- Declare locators as class fields. Prefer role, label, then placeholder, then test id.
- Expose actions and page-level assertions. Specs must not use raw locators.

```typescript
// BAD
async login(page: Page, email: string) {
  await page.locator('#email').fill(email);
}

// GOOD
readonly emailInput = this.page.getByLabel(/email/i);

async login(email: string, password: string) {
  await this.emailInput.fill(email);
  await this.passwordInput.fill(password);
  await this.submitButton.click();
}
```
